Subject:

Critical Issue: Custom HTML/JavaScript blocks being stripped or non-functional in Avada Builder
Message:

Hi Avada Team,

I am developing a high-end transportation platform (OnlyTransfer) and I am facing a critical issue with the Avada Builder.

The Problem:
I am trying to implement a simple redirection form (Input + Button) to send users to a sub-domain Web App. Every time I use a "Code Block" or a "Custom HTML" element to insert a basic <form> with a GET method or a simple JavaScript window.location.href, the code is either stripped or the button becomes non-functional after saving.

What I need:
I need to allow a simple input field where the user types a 8-digit code (e.g., B7K2P9WR) and, upon clicking the button, it redirects them to:
https://app.onlytransfer.eu/#/reserva?id=USER_CODE

Technical Environment:

    Avada Version: Latest

    WordPress Version: Latest

    Caching: Cleared

    Plugin Conflicts: None found

Could you please specify the "Avada-way" to implement a simple external redirection based on user input without the builder breaking the script or the form action?

Best regards,
Jordi Fabregat
CEO, OnlyTransfer
